.TH FATHOM_WATCH 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-watch \- Watch the repository and index as it changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom watch\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-once\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-cycles\fR] [\fB\-\-deadline\fR] [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-debounce\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-heartbeat\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-chunk\-units\fR] [\fB\-\-worktree\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-status\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIROOT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Watch the repository and index as it changes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON object per state change on stdout, and nothing else there
.TP
\fB\-\-once\fR
Index once, then exit: what a script or a CI check wants from `watch`
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-cycles\fR \fI<MAX_CYCLES>\fR
Stop after this many looks at the filesystem
.TP
\fB\-\-deadline\fR \fI<DEADLINE>\fR
Stop after this many seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR [default: auto]
Which change source to use: `auto`, `notify` or `poll`
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR \fI<INTERVAL_MS>\fR
The debounced polling interval in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-debounce\-ms\fR \fI<DEBOUNCE_MS>\fR
The quiescence window in milliseconds: how long the filesystem must be quiet before a change is read
.TP
\fB\-\-heartbeat\-ms\fR \fI<HEARTBEAT_MS>\fR
The liveness beat in milliseconds: how often the state is rewritten while nothing changes
.TP
\fB\-\-chunk\-units\fR \fI<CHUNK_UNITS>\fR [default: 2000]
Analysis units per index chunk — the watcher\*(Aqs slice of the CPU
.TP
\fB\-\-worktree\fR
Also re\-index uncommitted paths when only the index moved
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-status\-file\fR
Do not write `.fathom/watch/status.json`
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing to stdout but errors; the state machine still goes to the status file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIROOT\fR] [default: .]
The repository to watch
